id: pm-o0sqz5
title: "Recursive self-improvement loop: the immutable record selects, gates, and re-measures the next improvement to pm itself, so each cycle proves a number moved"
description: "Establish pm as its own measured improvement environment: immutable evidence selects a candidate, a tracked cycle proposes and gates a change, and the resulting metric is re-measured. Compose existing recurrence, escape, dogfood, trajectory, cost, and token surfaces so every cycle can prove whether pm improved and by how much."
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-loop,measurement,self-improvement,strategy
created_at: "2026-08-05T18:09:34.908Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T14:27:26.894Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: "A declared cycle exists — observe, propose, gate, land, re-measure — whose every turn is a tracked item carrying a receipt naming the metric, the baseline, and the post-change value; Candidate selection is derived from evidence already in the record rather than from filing recency; Every shipped cycle can answer, from tracked data alone, whether pm got better and by how much; The loop composes the existing measurement surfaces rather than duplicating them: the population ratchet, the defect-recurrence gate, the escape ratchet, the dogfood ratchet, trajectory projection, and the token corpus"
goal: measured recursive self-improvement
objective: "Turn immutable project evidence into a safe observe, propose, gate, land, and re-measure loop implemented entirely through public SDK contracts"
value: "pm improves from its own recorded outcomes while remaining falsifiable, reviewable, reversible by compensating events, and protected against Goodhart effects"
why_now: "The tracker already records recurrence, escape, output-cost, graph, release, and evaluation measurements, but selection and post-change comparison are still separate human procedures rather than one replayable improvement cycle."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: medium
