comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T18:10:28.694Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing (2026-08-05): searched the full corpus for recursive self improvement, self-improvement loops, and 'pm improves itself using its own tracker data'. The hits are all narrower and all real neighbours rather than duplicates — pm-cc04 is an ADR for agent self-repair through a remediation registry, pm-dhrp was a validation auto-fix session, pm-0682l4 and pm-k9t17l are self-reference guards in install and ordering. Nothing composes the measurement surfaces into a cycle.\n\nWhat exists is substrate, not a loop: pm-ips23h ratchets filed populations so they cannot grow, pm-1qkivy turns resolved incident patterns into gates, pm-rtn5h6 requires every escaped defect to land the gate that would have caught it, pm-pww8ax ratchets dogfood coverage, pm-qd6gvf projects the record as trajectories, pm-8pnj measures tokens per completed task, pm-2vs1za compares measured cost against forecast value. Each answers one question about one pass. None answers 'is pm getting better, by how much, measured how' across passes.\n\nThe asymmetry that motivates the ledger child: a ceiling can only ever prove a number did not grow. Every measurement the project ratchets is therefore blind to improvement — the one direction the loop needs to observe."
  "2026-08-15T13:58:30.893Z","harness:codex","Recursive improvement control loop: observe immutable operational, quality, token, latency, reliability, security, and user/agent outcome measures; attribute candidate causes from typed history and recurrence families; propose a bounded change with explicit hypothesis, affected population, cost, rollback-by-new-event plan, and protected invariants; rank it against alternatives and no-change; execute in an isolated branch/environment; run repository-owned negative controls, held-out evals, counterfactual replay, and exact-artifact checks; land only when the causal metric target improves without protected-metric regression; then remeasure production and feed the result back as append-only evidence. Separate proposer, evaluator, and policy authority so the system cannot approve its own unobserved claims. Use sequential tests or confidence intervals for noisy metrics, change-point detection for regressions, Pareto/frontier decisions for multi-objective tradeoffs, and explicit cost displacement so token savings that move cost elsewhere do not count as improvement. Guard against Goodhart behavior with rotating held-out suites, contamination/leakage checks, human policy constraints, population-adequacy proofs, novelty caps, and stop conditions. Every cycle is reproducible from SDK events and can be restored or reversed only by a new compensating event; no history rewrite, silent waiver, non-terminal external check, or unverifiable model judgment is treated as success."
  "2026-08-15T14:17:55.113Z","harness:codex","CI feedback on 2026-08-15 proved the direct blocked_by pm-o2kc edge was transitively redundant: the same prerequisite is already expressed by pm-o2kc -> pm-4k6b -> pm-o0sqz5. The direct edge was removed to preserve the deeper causal path and graph reduction ceiling; the recursive-improvement architecture and storage prerequisite remain fully represented."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-14T10:20:06.292Z","harness:codex","Recursive improvement operating model. Observe from immutable measurements, defect recurrence, release incidents, user friction, token cost, graph bottlenecks, and evaluation failures. Synthesize a ranked candidate with evidence, uncertainty, expected value, blast radius, and a falsifiable metric hypothesis. Materialize the candidate as a canonical item after all-status duplicate and lineage checks; generate a bounded implementation and verification plan; execute only inside the authority and sandbox declared by that item; run local and hosted gates against the exact change; then compare the same metric definition and corpus before and after. Land, reject, or revert based on the declared threshold, never on narrative confidence, and store the full receipt and trajectory so the next cycle can learn from both success and failure. Anti-Goodhart constraints require invariant safety and feature-parity gates, held-out evaluation scenarios, no ratchet weakening, and explicit accounting for displaced cost. The loop may propose work autonomously but cannot expand authority, bypass review or release policy, fabricate dependencies, or mutate history outside normal SDK primitives."
  "2026-08-22T07:18:09.433Z","harness:codex","Recursive improvement portfolio design, 2026-08-22. The loop is a graph of independently governed artifacts: an observation names a versioned population and measurement; a hypothesis predicts a bounded improvement and possible displaced costs; a decision records authority and acceptance thresholds; an implementation item owns changes; verification items provide positive, negative, and regression evidence; a release fact binds the exact artifact; and a post-change measurement compares the same definition and corpus. Typed discovered_from, implements, verifies, blocked_by, recurs_from, and supersedes edges make the cycle replayable without collapsing it into one mega-item.\n\nCandidate selection combines severity, recurrence, affected population, expected value, uncertainty, strategic reachability, blocker centrality, implementation cost, and evidence freshness under a portfolio capacity budget. It explicitly diversifies across domains and reserves capacity for security, reliability, debt, user value, and exploratory research. Selection cannot create work until an all-status duplicate and supersession check identifies the canonical owner. No metric may be optimized by weakening its denominator, threshold, negative control, or neighboring invariant; every promoted cycle carries a guardrail vector and a rollback or compensating-event path.\n\nLong-term maturity progresses from replayable human-driven cycles, to SDK-generated candidate and plan artifacts, to simulation and counterfactual evaluation, to bounded autonomous execution inside declared authority, and finally to federated learning across privacy-separated workspaces. Human review remains mandatory wherever policy, risk, external side effects, or irreversible authority changes demand it. Success is measured by sustained improvement in task success, escaped-defect recurrence, recovery closure, release reliability, context utility, token cost, lead time, and evidence completeness, not by number of changes or items created."
  "2026-08-24T14:27:26.894Z","harness:codex","Recursive improvement operating model after outcome-ladder closure: observe from immutable assurance, recurrence, escape, cost, latency, token, and user-outcome measurements; synthesize candidates from measured gaps rather than filing recency; select with a constrained multi-objective policy over expected value, uncertainty, risk, blocked fan-out, reversibility, and opportunity cost; generate the smallest negative control that proves the proposed gate can fail; execute only through public SDK primitives and normal reviewed delivery; remeasure the exact pre-change metric on merged code and published consumers; record a durable disposition for success, no-effect, regression, or confounding; feed that result back into candidate priors without rewriting the original evidence. Safety invariants are no self-modification outside tracked work, no reward shaping inside the core verdict contract, no metric promotion without an anti-Goodhart check, and automatic rollback or quarantine when a guarded metric regresses."
body: ""
